2d:["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","section","0",{"className":"grid gap-4 border-t border-fg pt-5 pb-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,4fr)_minmax(0,8fr)] lg:gap-[var(--gut)]","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-title max-w-[16ch] text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.4vw,2.2rem)]","children":"Context"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[66ch] space-y-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.62]","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":["Brazilian readers are stuck between catalogs that don't talk to each other: Skoob has the Brazilian titles but the product stalled years ago; Goodreads ignores Brazil; neither has a real habit loop. LIVRA is a gamified reading journal (streaks, weekly leagues, a coin economy, focus mode) built for readers who already turn books into content on TikTok and Instagram."]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section","1",{"className":"grid gap-4 border-t border-fg pt-5 pb-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,4fr)_minmax(0,8fr)] lg:gap-[var(--gut)]","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-title max-w-[16ch] text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.4vw,2.2rem)]","children":"The core technical problem"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[66ch] space-y-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.62]","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":["No single book-data source works for Brazil. Google Books has volume but is noisy and doesn't return page counts in search; Apple has the best covers but needs its locale forced; CBL is the authority on Brazilian editions but sometimes serves the catalog card as the cover; Open Library is only a fallback. None of them solves it alone. The orchestration is the product."]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section","2",{"className":"grid gap-4 border-t border-fg pt-5 pb-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,4fr)_minmax(0,8fr)] lg:gap-[var(--gut)]","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-title max-w-[16ch] text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.4vw,2.2rem)]","children":"What I built"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[66ch] space-y-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.62]","children":[["$","p","0",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":["A unified search that queries up to 6 sources in parallel, detects the query type (ISBN vs. free text) and reconciles everything into a canonical work × edition identity: the same book arriving as "]}],["$","code","1",{"className":"case-code","children":"apple-X"}],["$","$1","2",{"children":[", "]}],["$","code","3",{"className":"case-code","children":"google-Y"}],["$","$1","4",{"children":[" or "]}],["$","code","5",{"className":"case-code","children":"isbn:Z"}],["$","$1","6",{"children":[" converges on a single document. That prevents duplicate cards, fragmented reviews and inconsistent covers. Ratings are keyed by work, not edition, so different editions share the same reviews."]}]]}],["$","p","1",{"children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":["Around the core: a barcode-first scanner (local ZXing decode, zero cost) with multimodal AI only as a cover-photo fallback; recommendations generated by Gemini but validated against the real catalog before they become cards; and a self-healing catalog: opening a book with thin metadata triggers background enrichment, so browsing itself improves the database."]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section","3",{"className":"grid gap-4 border-t border-fg pt-5 pb-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,4fr)_minmax(0,8fr)] lg:gap-[var(--gut)]","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-title max-w-[16ch] text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.4vw,2.2rem)]","children":"Why it's built this way"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[66ch] space-y-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.62]","children":[["$","ul","0",{"className":"border-b border-line","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"border-t border-line py-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mb-1 block text-[0.9375rem] font-[680]","children":"Server-only economy"}],"$L32"]}],"$L33","$L34","$L35"]}]]}]]}],"$L36"]}]
